<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.2.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00724</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9d653e40-cc19-496f-993a-66821d1d3495</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use graphing technology to create a scatter plot and find the best fit line.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>What does the best fit line estimate for the \(y\)-value when \(x\) is 100?</item>
</list>

<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2213c4f6-63a8-43f1-88d4-65cbbcb95f2b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis> \(x\) </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> \(y\) </emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry> 83 </entry>
            <entry> 102 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 87 </entry>
            <entry> 115 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 91 </entry>
            <entry> 107 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 93 </entry>
            <entry> 122 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 97 </entry>
            <entry> 125 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 97 </entry>
            <entry> 127 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 101 </entry>
            <entry> 120 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry> 104 </entry>
            <entry> 127 </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
    <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>100</para><para>125</para><para>150</para><para>120</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The line of best fit is \(y=1.089x+15.588\), so when \(x\) is 100, \(y\) is about 125.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.2.2 – 3.23.</para><para>The correct answer for the line of best fit is \(y=1.089x+15.588\), so when \(x\) is 100, \(y\) is about 125. 
      
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="c769c078-adf6-4f2f-bd88-1986cf4d4423" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The best fit line is given by the equation \(y=0.404x−5.18\), where \(y\) represents the height of the
        plant above ground level, and \(x\) represents the number of days since it was planted.</para><para>A seed is planted in a glass pot, and its height is measured in centimeters every day.</para>
      <figure><media alt="A scatter plot. Horizontal, 0 to 30, by 1’s, labeled days. Vertical, negative 5 to 3, by point 5’s, labeled height in centimeters. 21 dots trend linearly up and to the right with a line a best fit."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/81da6887d175f5dd827e61bafa3f8293c749e3ad"/></media></figure><para>What is the slope of the best fit line? What does the slope of the line mean in this situation? </para>
    <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>The slope is 5.18, which means for every day, the plant grows 5.18 centimeters.</para><para>The slope is 0.404, which means for every day, the plant grows 0.404 centimeters. </para><para>The slope is -5.18, which means for every day, the plant shrinks -5.18 centimeters. </para><para>The slope is 0.404, which means the plant grows 1 centimeter every 0.404 days.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The slope is 0.404, which means for every day, the plant grows 0.404 centimeters. </para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.2.2 – 3.2.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: The slope is 0.404, which means for every day, the plant grows 0.404 centimeters. </para></solution></exercise></section><para>Use the following information to answer questions 3 - 5. </para>
<para><quote>The scatter plots below show different lines that students used to model the relationship between body mass
    (in pounds) and bite force (in pounds) for crocodiles.</quote><quote>Match each graph to one of the equations below, and explain your reasoning. Let \(B\) represent bite force (in
    pounds) and \(W\) represent body mass (in pounds).</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2a497ced-dbcd-445e-ac8d-01255b47f460" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which graph represents data that could be modeled by the equation,
          \(B = 3.28W + 126\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Line 3 and Equation 1 match because the intercept of Equation 1 is the smallest, which seems to match
        the graph. </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.2.1.</para><para>The correct answer is: Line 3 and Equation 1 match because the intercept of Equation 1 is the smallest, which
        seems to match the graph. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="7c1ce9c3-b22a-497d-b5f0-292bb5e4b48a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which graph represents data that could be modeled by the equation,
          \(B = 3.04W + 351\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Line 2 and Equation 2 match because the intercept of Equation 2 is larger, so it matches Line 2, which
        has a \(y\)-intercept closer to 400.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.2.1.</para><para>The correct answer is: Line 2 and Equation 2 match because the intercept of Equation 2 is larger, so it matches
        Line 2, which has a \(y\)-intercept closer to 400. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="970607b5-89fc-4744-8890-a013a6d9f3fa" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which graph represents data that could be modeled by the equation,
          \(B = 2.16W + 267\)? </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Line 1 and Equation 3 match because the intercept of 267 appears to match the graph, which has
        the second-largest intercept.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.2.1.</para><para>The correct answer is: Line 1 and Equation 3 match because the intercept of 267 appears to match the graph,
        which has the second-largest intercept. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="f2e32e15-3966-494b-b130-e03c979a9bfe" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following equations is a linear model representing the number of yards, \(Y\), Mike can cut in \(x\) days.</para><para>Mike owns a grass cutting business. The table below shows how many yards, \(Y\), he can cut in \(x\) days.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Number of days, x</emphasis></entry><entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Number of yards cut, Y</emphasis></entry><entry>6</entry>
            <entry>12</entry>
            <entry>18</entry>
            <entry>24</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(Y=6x\)</para><para>\(Y=6x+6\)</para><para>\(Y=\frac16x\)</para><para>\(Y=\frac16x+6\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(Y =6d\)</para><para>Since the change in \(y\) is 6 and change in \(x\) is 1, the slope is 6. Working backwards, when \(x = 0\), \(Y=0\) so the equation becomes \(Y=6x+0\) or \(Y = 6x\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.2.3. </para><para>The correct answer is \(Y = 6x\)</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
